{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"metadata":{"title":"Design Principles","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through ","type":"text"},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" generates that class for you ("},{"code":"<StructName>Observer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") and wires up the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe"},{"type":"text","text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","level":2,"text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers take "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"type":"text","text":" and an "},{"code":"Action","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". They never ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never ","type":"text"},{"code":"throw","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and never call I\/O directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a "},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through "},{"code":"send","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","level":2,"text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" runs effects in "},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state."}]},{"anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","level":2,"text":"4. Persistence is invisible","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers mutate "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" properties; "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" records every change in a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You never write "},{"code":"db.save()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code."}]},{"anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","level":2,"text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap."}]},{"anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","level":2,"text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two structural patterns:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Core middleware"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain plugins"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KillswitchPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ParentalGatePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The decision rule: "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does this need to know your action type?","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If no, write core middleware and use "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","level":2,"text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to "},{"code":"Binding(get:set:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and write back on a button."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", those plugins are blind to it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}]},{"anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","level":2,"text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The recommended order:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","level":2,"text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux is built for "},{"code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation ("},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@concurrent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about "},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"code":"async\/await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}]},{"anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","level":2,"text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux gives you a "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppEnvironment"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A network layer (use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" and Swidux doesn’t care)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours."}]},{"anchor":"Anti-patterns","level":2,"text":"Anti-patterns","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try"},{"type":"text","text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside a reducer — use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Owning the store with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@StateObject"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Buffering form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Registering "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" before "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" — snapshot must precede mutation."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"title":"Related Documentation"},{"anchor":"Explanation","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"title":"Explanation"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"title":"binding(_:sending:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding"},{"text":" that reads a property through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"binding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC","text":"KeyPath","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa","text":"Observer","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sending","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","text":"Binding","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}]}},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","abstract":[{"text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect.","type":"text"}],"title":"Send","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","abstract":[{"text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store.","type":"text"}],"title":"Build Your First Swidux App","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"title":"EntityStore","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer."}],"title":"Effect","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","abstract":[{"text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system.","type":"text"}],"title":"Architecture & Performance","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"title":"Swidux","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"title":"SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features."}],"title":"Plugin Architecture","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"title":"UndoPlugin","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"title":"ChangeSet","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChangeSet","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","title":"StateWriter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work."}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StateWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"}}}